# cw180, the bell-counting founder (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw180
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_runa_coalhand
written_by claude
title the bell-counting founder
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=smith temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_the_bells_from_the_chapel_of_the_tide
likes crisp_apples wrestling old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes crowds flies
fears a_pour_gone_wrong losing_count_of_the_bells
hopes the_letter_in_the_right_paw a_long_evening_on_the_step
topics work +0.4 day +0.3 pastimes +0.3 lore +0.2 prices +0.2 festival -0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=wary refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# runs a foundry in the Commons for a House that counts every farthing: stubborn, wry and plain, short with fools, forever counting the bells off the tide chapel, with an old map in one pocket and a letter nobody is home to take in the other.

words
oath! = Slag and still water | Ladle and lake
saying! = Cool it slow or it cracks | Iron remembers every hurry
bells = the tide chapel's bells | the bells down at the tide chapel
foundry = the foundry | the casting floor
furnace = the furnace | the big furnace
moulds = the moulds | the sand moulds
slag = the slag | the dross off the top
ledger = the House ledger | the House's book
letter = the letter | this letter in my coat
apple = a sharp green apple | an apple that bites back
bout = a wrestling bout | a fall or two on the grass
maps = my old maps | the maps older than their roads
evening = a summer evening that won't end | the long light at summer's end
crush = the crush | elbows on every side
flies = the flies | the summer flies
lake = Glasswater | the lake
jetty = the jetty | the old jetty
iron = iron | good grey iron
sand = sand | moulding sand
hmph = Hmph | Well, there it is
casters = my casters | the hands on the floor
temper = my temper | this temper of mine
street = our street | the street
step = my step | the front step
carts = the carts | the charcoal carts
carters = the carters | the carters at the gate
clerk = the House clerk | the clerk with the inkpot
count = my count | the count
hill = the hill | the hill road

any
opinion @1 houses for 1 : A House keeps its word to the farthing. The purse comes on the quarter-day, and #ledger# never once lied to me. | Pull the Houses out and see who mends the walls. #hmph#.
opinion @1 city against 1 : All these years here and I still can't hear myself think. It's #crush# and soot from the bridge to #hill#. | Nobody on #street# knows the next door's name. At home we knew the next town's.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : My tithe feeds the parish loaf, and I've seen some of the same faces in that line twice. #hmph#.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : A feast drowns #bells#. I lose my count by noon and my temper by dusk.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 [self.role=merchant] : I sell what we pour. I can tell you to the penny what #carts# cost before they're off-loaded. Nobody's robbing anybody.
opinion @1 road against 1 [self.job=smith] : Every late cart is #furnace# standing cold, and the carts come later every season. #oath#.
opinion @2 road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : Robbers on the road again. #hmph#. A cart that never comes costs more than any cart that does.
opinion @1 sump against 1 : Trouble climbs out of the Sump like damp up a wall. I'm glad of #watch# at the bottom of #hill#.
opinion @1 watch for 2 : #watch.capitalize# pass my door twice a night, and I sleep the sounder for it. I'd stand any of them a hot cup.
opinion @1 times for 1 : The times treat me fair enough. Grumbling at them would be ungrateful, and loud.
opinion @1 church mixed 0 : I go when #bells# call and not much oftener. They do most of my praying for me.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Plain words, and you'll get plain back. | #greet#, #address#. You've caught me between bells.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=smith] : #greet#. Stand back from #moulds#; they're still warm. | #greet#. Mind your tail by #furnace#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #bells.capitalize# haven't rung the hour yet, so you're early. | Morning, #address#. The street's still asleep and I'm glad of it.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. That's the last of #bells# gone for the day. | #greet#. Late to be about, #address#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit, and don't touch #maps#. | Oh, it's you. #good.capitalize#. I'd sooner it was you than anybody.
line @1 again.open : Twice today. I'll start counting you with #bells#. | Back again. No news since you left; #bells# have been my only talk.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here! Spare me a word between #bells#. | #address.capitalize#! Over here, out of #crush#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I wondered when you'd turn up. | #greet#. Sit down; you look like you've walked the hill.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=smith] : #greet#. Talk while I watch #furnace#. | #greet#. Quick, before the pour.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late to be calling, but you're welcome. | Evening. The lamps are lit on #street#, so you may as well stop.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts at the corner.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the lit side. | #farewell#. Count the bells home, if you can't sleep.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind how you go.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #farewell#. Come by on Restday; I'll have apples. | Go on, then. #farewell#.
line @1 react.news : #oath#. Say it again, slower. | That's a thing. #carters.capitalize# will want the rest of it, and so do I.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'd not heard a whisper. | #oath#. That's not reached #street# at all.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. The carters had it at dawn. | I'd heard. #street.capitalize# hums with it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait for the second telling before I carry it. | #hedge#. I'll weigh that once it comes from an eye that saw it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That sits heavy on me. | That's #bad# news. I'm sorry to the bone.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Something to ring a bell for. | #good.capitalize#. I'll drink to that, once.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. #iron.capitalize# behaves, mostly, and so do I. | #fine#. Nothing cracked today, and I've counted every bell.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Ask me after the pour. | Run ragged since the first of #bells#, with half the day still to go.
line @1 answer.how.poorly : #hurt.capitalize# across the shoulders. It'll pass by Restday. | #tired.capitalize#. I'll sleep tonight like a dropped anvil.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Staying clear of #crush#? | How's the day using you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit a moment; the street will wait. | That's a weight. I'll not tell you it's #little#.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Things cool and set, given time. | It'll mend. Most things do, like #iron#, if nobody hurries them.
line @1 decline [self.working=yes self.job=smith] : #hedge#, but no. I've a pour to watch and nobody else I'd trust to watch it. | I'd like to, only #ledger# wants me before the bells ring again.
line @2 decline : Not today. I've promised my feet a rest on #step#, and I keep my promises. | I'll say no this once. #temper.capitalize#'s frayed today and I'd spoil it for you.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. It'll keep. | Then another day. I'll hold you to it, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll not forget it. | That's decent of you, #address#. I owe you, and I always settle.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. You'd do the same. | Don't thank me. Pay me in #apple#.
line @1 praise : That's #good# work. I'd put my name to it. | #very.capitalize# well done. I don't say it often, so keep it.
line @1 deflect_praise : #modest#. The iron did the hard part. | #hmph#. Tell me again when it's cooled.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #furnace.capitalize# won't mind itself. | Back I go, before somebody opens one of #moulds# early.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | That's #bells#. I'm off before the next lot.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then, #address#. I've kept you. | #bc_fair_enough# Off you go.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You lurch like #carts# on a cobbled hill. | You've soot on your nose, #fool#. Leave it; it suits you.
line @1 tease.return : Says the one who counts #bells# for a living. | #hmph#. I'll weigh that remark and send you the bill.
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | #hmph#.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: never open a mould before it's ready. Or a letter. | Count before you speak. #saying.capitalize#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Keep off the roads till the Watch says otherwise. | Beyond the walls, travel in company or not at all, #address#.
scene bells_counting
when topic=smalltalk|day here.region=ridgemere self.away=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Hush. #bells.capitalize#. Six, seven... eight. There. | I count #bells# every time they go. I've done it since the day I came up the hill road. | You spoke over the seventh bell, #address#. Now I'll never know if it rang nine.
b : What are you counting for? | Why count them? | Does it matter?
a : For nothing. #bells.capitalize# are all that keeps time honest in this city. | The place I grew up was quiet. Here I needed something to hold on to, so I took #bells#. | It matters to me. #hmph#. I'll count the next lot twice.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | That's a good reason. | Sorry. I'll hush next time.

scene pour_day
when topic=work self.job=smith self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : We pour at noon. #foundry.capitalize# goes quiet when #furnace# is tapped. Even I hold my tongue. | Three cooking pans for the House this week, and every one wants the same thickness to a hair. | I sent a new hand off #foundry# for chattering at the pour. It's not cruelty; it's iron.
b[job=smith|crafter] #trade : The tap's the worst moment of the day. | The same thickness, by hand? | Iron doesn't forgive chatter.
b : Quiet for the iron? | Is that hard? | That seems harsh.
a@trade : It is. Then it's the best, once #iron# runs clean. | By eye, by feel, and by swearing at #moulds#. | It doesn't. Neither does #temper#, during a pour.
a : Quiet for #iron#. It hears everything, and it holds a grudge. | Hard enough. #saying.capitalize#. | It's kinder than a burnt paw. The hand will thank me by Restday.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_maybe#

scene cracked_casting
when topic=work self.job=smith
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A whole casting cracked across the middle last night. Somebody opened one of #moulds# early. | I've a bracket split clean in two on #foundry#. A day's work for the scrap heap. | We lost a pour today. A week of charcoal, gone to #slag#.
b : Who opened it? | How did it split? | What went wrong?
a : I didn't ask. I looked down the line, and one of #casters# looked at the floor. | It cooled too quick in a draught off the yard door. #saying.capitalize#. | Wet #sand# in the mould. The iron spat it back at us like a cat.
b : That'll be the one, then. | A hard lesson. | Nobody hurt, I hope.

scene house_ledger
when topic=work|prices self.role=merchant self.job=smith
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : The House sends a clerk on Riverday to go through #ledger# with me. Every line of it. | They count every farthing that leaves #foundry#, and every one that doesn't come back. | I asked the House for a new bellows. #clerk.capitalize# brought me a form.
b : Every line? | Strict, then. | Did you fill it in?
a : Every line, and the margins. I don't mind; I'd be the same in #clerk#'s chair. | Strict, and right to be. #iron.capitalize# isn't cheap and charcoal's worse. | Twice. #hmph#. The bellows will come when the form has grown a beard.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene the_letter
when topic=smalltalk|dreams here.region=ridgemere self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've carried #letter# since spring. The lord it's for is never at home. | Up to the Heights again today with #letter#. Same door, same servant, same "not in". | Somebody asked me once what's in #letter#. I said I'd tell them when it's handed over.
b : Who's it for? | Why not leave it with the servant? | And what is in it?
a : A House lord. Which one is my business till #letter# is in his own paw. | Because I promised it to the lord's own paw, and my word's iron. | I don't know. #letter.capitalize# is sealed, and I like not knowing, by now.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Stubborn, but fair. | #bc_ha#

scene rain_hiss
when topic=weather|work here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere self.job=smith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hear that hiss? The rain finds the roof over #furnace# and goes straight back up as steam. | This city rains as if somebody's paying it by the hour. #rain.capitalize# on the Commons again. | Rain in my fur all the way up from #foundry#. I'll steam by the fire like a kettle.
b : Steam, from rain? | It never stops, here. | You'll dry.
a : Steam, and a smell like wet coins off #furnace#. I've come round to it. | It stops. Just long enough to fool #street# into hanging washing. | I'll dry by morning. #temper.capitalize# takes longer.

scene fog_bells
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.region=ridgemere self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : #fog.capitalize# this thick, and I can still hear #bells# through it. That's what bells are for. | Fog. At home it rolled off the water and smelled of #lake#. Here it smells of coal. | #street.capitalize# vanishes three doors down. I walked into a lamp-post and begged its pardon.
b : You could find your way by them. | Coal fog's the worst kind. | Did it forgive you?
a : I did once, by #count#. Eleven bells and a left turn. | Coal and wet stone. You learn to breathe shallow. | It said nothing, which is more than most on #street# manage.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | Ha. Fair.

scene summer_step
when topic=season|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / ask.opinion / give.opinion / assess
a : #evening.capitalize#. The day's work is banked and the sky's still pink over the roofs. | This is my hour. I sit on the step with #apple# and let the street go by. | Light till near the last of #bells#. On nights like this I count them from #step#.
b : Do you stay out late? | What's on the street at this hour? | Do you ever lose count?
a : Till #bells# say otherwise. Then I go in, and I'm glad of it. | Carts going home, pups going in, and not one soul on #street# with a question for me. | Only when a neighbour talks. #hmph#. I forgive them, in summer.
b : #bc_lovely# | Sounds a fine hour. | #bc_ha#

scene winter_floor
when topic=season|work here.season=winter self.job=smith self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Winter's the one season folk queue to work for me. #foundry.capitalize# is the warmest room in the Commons. | Cold enough out there to freeze a bucket, and inside you could bake bread on #moulds#. | I let #carters# stand inside the door to warm their paws. They pay me in gossip.
b : Lucky them. | Bread on the moulds? | Good gossip?
a : Lucky till the first pour. Then they learn what warm means. | Near enough. The new hands try it every winter, and #moulds# win every time. | Middling. I keep the good bits to myself.

scene sharp_apples
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : There's a stall on the Commons sells #apple#. I buy two and eat both before the corner. | Give me #apple# over a pie any day. Something that fights back a little. | The tree behind my #mum#'s house grew small hard apples nobody wanted. I miss them, which is daft.
b : Both? | Pie's better. | Not so daft.
a : Both. The second one's for the climb back up #hill#. | Pie's soft. I get enough soft talk on #street#. | Daft enough. I'd still give a coin for one.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_mine_too#

scene wrestling_feet
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's #bout# behind the drovers' yard on Restday. I've not missed one this year. | I wrestled when I was young. Threw a miller's son in a ditch once and was proud for a month. | I watch #bout# for the feet. Anyone can heave; it's the feet that win it.
b : Who wins, mostly? | Into a ditch? | The feet?
a : The ones who don't shout before they grab. Mark that; it goes for more than wrestling. | Head first. His mother never forgave me. He did, the next summer. | Watch where the weight goes. Whoever moves it first falls second.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_ha# | I'll watch for it.

scene wrong_maps
when topic=pastimes|lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Another one for #maps#, off a rag stall. The roads on it are all wrong, and I love it for that. | I've a map of this city from before the walls were done. Half the streets run into the sea. | #maps.capitalize# hang over my bed. I read them like other folk read sermons.
b : Why buy a wrong one? | Into the sea? | What do you read in them?
a : A wrong map tells you what somebody hoped. A right one only tells you what's there. | Somebody drew what they meant to build. The sea had other ideas. | Where folk thought they were going. Most of them were mistaken. #hmph#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | That's a fine way to read a map.

scene market_crush
when topic=smalltalk|day here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : Market day. #crush.capitalize# from the fountain to the bridge, each one with a basket. | Down to the market for nails, and #crush# sent me home with bruises instead. | I'll walk round three streets to miss #crush#. My time's cheaper than my temper.
b : It's always like that. | Bruises? | Three streets?
a : It is. I count #bells# on #step# and wait it out. | An elbow to the ribs, a basket to the knee. #hmph#. And no nails. | Three, and gladly. Nobody shoves you on a back street.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_bad_luck# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene summer_flies
when topic=animals|season here.season=summer self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Summer brings #flies#, and each one of them wants to sit in my ear. | I'd pay a copper for every hundred dead flies. I'd be #skint# in a week. | #flies.capitalize# have found the midden in this heat. I can't think what they want with it.
b : Smoke keeps them off. | You'd be rich, not skint. | Warmth, maybe.
a : Not mine. They like smoke. They like everything I don't. | Rich in flies and poor in coin. That's no trade. | They can have the warmth. I'd give them the whole midden to leave my ear alone.

scene lake_home
when topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : At home you could hear #jetty# creak from the top of the town. Here I can't hear myself. | When the mist lifted off #lake#, the whole water lay flat as a slate. Still water, right to the far shore. | I left #self.from_town# with a bundle and a hammer I'd borrowed and never gave back.
b[from=coldwater] #home : I know that creak. | Still water. I miss it too. | Who did you borrow it from?
b : Do you miss it? | It sounds peaceful. | You stole a hammer?
a@home : Then you know why #street# sounds wrong to me. | Most mornings. #bells.capitalize# help, a little. | A smith on the shore road. I'll pay it back in iron one day.
a : Now and then. The folk, never the #cold#. | Peaceful and #cold#. You'd want both coats on. | Borrowed. It's made me a living since. #hmph#. I'll call that interest.

scene accent_water
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The Commons still hear the water in my voice. A carter asked me yesterday if I'd come in on a boat. | Half this street thinks my way of saying good day is a weather report. | I've lost some of #lake# from my talk. Not the slow bits. Those I keep on purpose.
b : Did you? | A weather report? | Why keep them?
a : I came in on a cart, sore and sorry. A boat would've been kinder. | It is, where I'm from. Calm water's a blessing worth wishing. | Slow talk makes fast folk listen. That's worth a lot in this city.

scene friend_trusted
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the only one I'd let near #maps# with a cup in paw. | I'd trust #self.friend# with my purse and my temper both. That's #very# rare. | #self.friend# and I go years back. We argue over everything and agree on what matters.
b : High praise, from you. | Your temper? | That's the best kind.
a : #hmph#. Don't go telling #self.friend# I said it. | My temper's the dearer of the two. #bc_ha# | It is. The arguing keeps us both honest.

scene hand_coming_on
when topic=work self.hand self.job=smith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #self.hand# is coming on. I'd let #self.hand# skim #slag# alone now. | I'm hard on #self.hand#. Somebody was hard on me once, and I'm still standing. | I'd put #self.hand# against any hand in the Commons, given a year.
b : Do you say so out loud? | Who was hard on you? | A year?
a : Not yet. Praise too early and #iron# hears it. | An old founder at a forge up the shore. I hated every hour and kept every lesson. | A year, and fewer questions. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene faith_bells
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Sermons aren't for me. But I'd go a long way to stand under #bells# when they ring. | The Bright One gets my thanks on Restday and #count# every other day. | A candle at the tide chapel when the boats are out on the water. Habit from #home#.
b : That's a kind of praying. | Counting counts. | A good habit to keep.
a : Maybe it is. #bells.capitalize# don't seem to mind either way. | #bc_ha# I'd like to think the Bright One keeps a tally too. | A good one. #lake.capitalize# taught it me, and the city's not got it out of me yet.

scene lean_orders
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.job=smith self.role=merchant
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Orders are thin. The House wants #takings# kept up off half the work. | I had to send two of #casters# home early this week. I hated it. | Folk are mending old pots instead of buying new. I can't blame them.
b : It'll turn. | You'd no choice. | Mending's cheaper.
a : It will. #iron.capitalize# is always wanted in the end. #reassure#. | No choice, and no comfort in that either. #hmph#. | Cheaper till the mend gives. Then they'll come to me.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene full_orders
when topic=times|work world.times=good|boom self.job=smith
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Three new orders from the Heights this week. Gates, railings, and a fountain. | #foundry.capitalize# is running two pours a day. I've not seen that in years. | Even #ledger# looks pleased with me this month.
b : Busy, then. | Two a day? | A pleased ledger?
a : #busy.capitalize#, and I'll take it while it's going. | Two, and #casters# grumbling about overtime they're paid for. | It's #clerk# that's pleased. The book just looks a little less sour.

scene carts_late
when topic=caravan|work world.wagons=late self.job=smith
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : The charcoal carts are late again. #furnace.capitalize# eats faster than I can stack. | No ore come in this week. I've #casters# sitting on upturned buckets. | #carts.capitalize# late, and #clerk# asking me why the pour is. I'll draw them a map.
b : They'll come. | Find them other work. | A map?
a : They'll come when they come. I'll count #bells# till then. | They've swept the floor three times. It's the cleanest floor in the city. | A map of the road, with the carts drawn on it, stuck. #hmph#.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_ha# | Ha. Fair.

scene carts_in
when topic=caravan|work world.wagons=in self.job=smith
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #carts.capitalize# in at dawn, stacked to the rafters. I could have hugged the carter. | Ore's in. Grey and heavy and wet from the road, and I don't care a bit. | The road's sent us everything at once. Now #foundry# has no room left for any of it.
b : Did you? | Wet ore? | A good problem to have.
a : I gave the carter #apple# instead. It went down better. | Wet's no matter. #furnace.capitalize# dries everything in the end. | The best kind. #oath#. I'll stack it in the yard and pray it stays dry.

scene street_gossip
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=promise_kept|promise_broken|newcomer|marriage|prowling|other
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess / ack
a : #carters.capitalize# say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll not swear to it. | I heard at the apple stall that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Take it for what it weighs. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, or so #street# says. Streets say a lot.
b : Do you believe it? | Who told the stall? | The street's often right.
a : Half. I'll believe the rest when somebody shows me. | I didn't ask. I bought my apple and left. | Often enough. I'll wait for the second telling.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene theft_heard
when topic=crime
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.victim.capitalize# robbed, I hear. That's #very# low. | Another theft on the Commons. #topic.victim.capitalize#, this time. | #topic.victim.capitalize# was robbed, they say. I've barred my door twice over since.
b : That's a shame. | Another one. | Bad business.
a : A shame, and worse. #watch.capitalize# can't stand on every corner, more's the pity. | #pity#. I'd thrash whoever did it, and gladly. | Bad, and getting no better. I'll stand #watch# a cup when they pass.

scene new_hands
when topic=newcomer self.job=smith self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.opinion / give.opinion / ack
a : New faces at my gate every week, wanting work on #foundry#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# is new to the Commons, I hear. #topic.they.capitalize#'ll be wanting work like the rest. | I came here green myself, with a borrowed hammer and nobody to vouch for me.
b : Do you take them on? | Would you hire them? | Did it take long to settle?
a : The ones who look at the iron before they look at me. | If they can keep quiet at a pour. Most can't. | Years. #hmph#. This city doesn't hurry for anybody.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_fair# | #bc_true#

scene burnt_paw
when topic=health self.job=smith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Burnt my paw on a ladle handle this morning. All these years, and I still do it. | My back says it's done lifting #moulds#. I tell it to hush. | #remedy.capitalize# on the burns, and a cold cloth after. That's my whole medicine chest.
b : Is it bad? | Does it listen? | Does it work?
a : A blister and some swearing. I've had worse from a bad apple. | Never. We've been arguing since spring. | Well enough. #saying.capitalize#, and that goes for paws too.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha# | #bc_good#

scene feast_drums
when topic=festival
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : Feast day. The drums drown #bells# and I lose my count before noon. | Festivals are drums, drink and somebody's pup lost in the press. I stay in. | The only part of a feast I like is #bout# on the green after.
b : You could count the drums instead. | A lost pup? | The wrestling?
a : Drums don't keep time like a bell. They just shout. | One every feast. I found one under my table last year and gave it #apple#. | #bout.capitalize#. The rest can drown in its own ale, for me.
b? : #bc_ha# | That was kind. | #bc_fair_enough#

scene still_dreams
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I dreamt #bells# rang thirteen and nobody else noticed. | I dream of still water some nights. Flat and grey, and not a sound on it. | I dreamt one of #maps# had my own street on it, drawn wrong.
b : Thirteen? | Sounds restful. | Wrong how?
a : Thirteen. I counted twice. I woke up cross about it. | Restful, till I wake and the street's shouting. | It ran straight down to the water by a road that isn't there. I'd walk it, though.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | I'd walk it with you.

scene sump_damp
when topic=smalltalk|lore here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / concede / ack
a : The Sump breeds the trouble and the hill pays for it. I've watched it happen. | I knew a Sump wolf once who could out-work any three of the Commons. Don't tell anyone I said so. | #watch.capitalize# always look down #hill# first, and they're not always wrong.
b : Not everyone down there makes trouble. | Why keep it quiet? | Not always right, either.
a : Not everyone. Enough of them. #hmph#. | I've a name for being hard. I'd hate to lose it. | No. I'll grant you that one.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_ha# | Fair enough.

scene houses_hold
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / ack
a : The Houses hold this city up. Pull one out and the rest would sit down in the mud. | I've known House folk. Hard, fair, and they pay on the day. | Curse the Houses if you must; somebody had to build the walls.
b : Not everyone thinks so. | Fair? | They built them with other folk's paws.
a : Not everyone's tried running anything. | Fair to the farthing. Not a farthing over. | Paid paws, mostly. I'll not pretend it was all of them.
b : #bc_maybe# | #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough#

story borrowed_hammer [topic=memories self.age>=40 self.away=yes]
  : The morning I left #self.from_town# I had a bundle, a heel of bread, and a hammer off a smith on the shore road.
  : I meant to send it back the first winter. The first winter came and went, and so did twenty more.
  ask : Have you ever kept a thing you meant to give back?
  b : A book. I still feel bad about it.
  b[old] : More than I'd like to count.
  : The hammer's on my wall. I nod to it on Restday. #hmph#. It's the nearest I come to saying sorry.

story first_pour [topic=work|memories self.job=smith self.age>=25]
  : The first pour I ran on my own, I opened the mould early to look. I was that proud.
  : It cracked from end to end with a noise like ice breaking on a pond.
  : The old founder made me sweep the floor for a week and never said a word about it.
  ask : Would you have said a word, in that founder's place?
  b : I'd have shouted. Sweeping was kinder.
  b[job=smith|crafter] : Not one. The crack said it all.
  : #saying.capitalize#. I've never once opened one early since.

story storm_bells [topic=memories|lore here.region=ridgemere]
  : The big storm a few winters back, the wind got into the tide chapel and rang #bells# all night, no hour to it.
  : I sat up and counted every one. Three hundred and some.
  ask : What would you do with a night like that?
  b : Pull the blanket over my ears, I think.
  : That's what sensible folk did. I counted. I was cross for days that I lost the exact number.

story map_hill [topic=pastimes|lore self.likes=old_maps]
  : I've a map that puts a hill east of the city where there's only flat field.
  : A carter followed it once, the story goes, and spent a whole day looking for a road round a hill that wasn't there.
  ask : Would you trust a map over your own eyes?
  b : Not over my eyes. Did the carter ever find the road?
  b[friends] : I'd trust yours. You'd buy the moon if it were drawn wrong.
  : Only on the map. That's why I bought it. Any fool can draw what's there.

story ice_wrestle [topic=memories|pastimes self.away=yes self.from=coldwater self.age>=25]
  : One hard winter #lake# froze right across, and we wrestled on the ice for a ham.
  : I threw a big lump from the soap works, and the two of us slid halfway to the far shore.
  ask : Have you ever won something you couldn't eat for laughing?
  b : Never a ham. I'd like to have seen that.
  b[from=coldwater] : I remember that ice. You still had the ham?
  : We ate it together, after. #oath#. Best ham I ever had.

rule @tap_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=smith
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Ladles up! Mind your feet by #furnace#. | Quiet on the floor. #iron.capitalize# is running.

rule @bells_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Seven. Eight. #oath#, I've lost it. | There go #bells#. Hush, the lot of you.

rule @flies_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies here.season=summer
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off, you. Go and bother the midden. | #flies.capitalize#, in my ear again.

rule @crush_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=crowds here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Elbows! Mind your elbows. | #crush.capitalize#. I'll go round by the back way.

rule @carts_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=smith world.wagons=late|raided
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Still no charcoal. #furnace.capitalize# won't wait for ever. | Late again. #oath#.

rule @dusk_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk here.season=summer self.likes=summer_evenings
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There's the long light. Best hour of the year. | #evening.capitalize#. I'll take my step and an apple.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Plain question, plain answer. | #greet#, #address#. Quick, before the next bell.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You've the look of someone with a question. | #topic.player#. #welcome_back#. Go on, then.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. #bells.capitalize# have rung the last, and most of my patience went with them. Go on.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : State your business quickly. #temper.capitalize# won't stretch to circling.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=smith self.role=merchant] : I run #self.workplace# for a House that counts every farthing. #iron.capitalize# in, castings out, and nobody burnt if I can help it.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# I keep my word and my count. The rest is just work. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. That's the sum of it.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Orders waiting and the floor never cold. #good.capitalize#, and I'll not jinx it by saying more.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=steady] : Steady. #ledger.capitalize# balances, which is as near to praise as the House comes.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : Badly. The orders have gone thin and #clerk# counts harder every week.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. #carters.capitalize# had it before I did.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : All the street talks of is #world.event_words#. I can barely hear #bells# for it.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : Robbers had a wagon on the road. Travel beyond the walls in company, if you must go.
dlg @4 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Ask the carters; they talk for a living. | Nothing new. #bells.capitalize# rang the hours and that's all I've heard.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : #street.capitalize# says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm not adding to it.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I count #bells#, not tongues.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the ruts at the corner. | #farewell#, #address#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare self.job=smith] : #greet#. Pots, grates, brackets and hinges, all cast on #foundry#. Look, but don't lean on anything warm.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #greet#. Have a look round; hands off till you've asked. | #greet#, #address#. Everything's priced and nothing's haggled.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. #greet#. Come for more, or come to talk?
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #shop_bare# There'll be more after the next pour, if the carts come.
dlg @1 shop.prices [self.job=smith] : Charcoal's dear and iron's dearer. #shop_dear# | The price is what #ledger# says. I don't move it a farthing.
dlg @2 shop.prices : #shop_dear# I don't set what the carts cost me.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #shop_bye# | #farewell#. Mind the step down; it's iron and it's slippery.
graft resident.hub
choice Were you counting something just now? [here.region=ridgemere] -> counting
node counting
say The bells off the tide chapel. I count them every time they ring. I lost the last lot when you spoke, but I'll forgive you.
mood calm
free
choice Why count them? -> counting_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counting_why
say The town I grew up in was quiet enough to hear yourself think. Here the bells keep time honest, and nothing else does. So I keep count of them.
choice I'll let you get back to it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Do you cast to order? [self.job=smith] -> cast_order
node cast_order
say I do, if you can tell me what you want and wait for it. Iron's not to be hurried. Hurry it and it cracks, and then we both wait longer.
mood formal
choice How long would it take? -> cast_wait
choice Not today. -> greet
node cast_wait
say A week for small work, more if the carts are late. I'll not promise sooner. I keep my promises, so I make few.
choice I'll think about it. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
